 "head": {
  "text": "WF-038 Hard synchronization on the recessive to dominant edge from FDF to res"
 },
 "foot": {
  "text": "In an FD frame the receiver hard-synchronizes at the edge from the FDF bit (recessive) to the res bit (dominant), even with a phase error, so that the data phase that follows starts from a fresh alignment (REF-002 rule 3). The same edge starts the delay measurement of the transmitter."
 }
